{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02634",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 4.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.45,
      "end_seconds": 11.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.21,
      "end_seconds": 22.88,
      "duration_seconds": 9.67,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got stiff aching shoulders and hips. I've been putting this off for weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.86,
      "end_seconds": 26.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Alright, I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.66,
      "end_seconds": 40.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.95,
      "end_seconds": 56.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 84, temperature is 36.7 degrees, BP is 127 over 75."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.91,
      "end_seconds": 59.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.25,
      "end_seconds": 66.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers. How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.89,
      "end_seconds": 74.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "Ever since... since Friday, really. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.95,
      "end_seconds": 77.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "I follow. Does anything help it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.86,
      "end_seconds": 94.16,
      "duration_seconds": 15.3,
      "text": "It settles a little with moving about. Oh, and difficulty getting out of bed. That's been about the same, one week. About difficulty getting out of bed, I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.25,
      "end_seconds": 99.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "A few quick ones: weight loss or headache?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.65,
      "end_seconds": 104.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.7,
      "end_seconds": 111.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "A few quick ones: visual changes or jaw pain on chewing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.5,
      "end_seconds": 117.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "No visual changes or jaw pain on chewing, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.01,
      "end_seconds": 121.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.07,
      "end_seconds": 130.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "No, um, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.22,
      "end_seconds": 133.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.51,
      "end_seconds": 135.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.36,
      "end_seconds": 149.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.23,
      "end_seconds": 160.6,
      "duration_seconds": 10.37,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother. I do a yoga class on Thursdays. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.41,
      "end_seconds": 164.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.01,
      "end_seconds": 169.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Migraines, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.46,
      "end_seconds": 174.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.28,
      "end_seconds": 181.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "Yes, I had a wisdom tooth extraction under sedation, five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.06,
      "end_seconds": 191.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.0,
      "end_seconds": 195.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.99,
      "end_seconds": 208.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.03,
      "end_seconds": 211.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "My sister had breast cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.11,
      "end_seconds": 224.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.0,
      "end_seconds": 232.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "I take sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed for my migraines. Propranolol I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.59,
      "end_seconds": 237.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.17,
      "end_seconds": 240.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.55,
      "end_seconds": 265.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.5,
      "text": "The shoulders are painful to move but strength is normal and there is no joint swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.89,
      "end_seconds": 279.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.83,
      "text": "Please sit back down. So, based on the history and the examination, I'd lean towards polymyalgia rheumatica. We shouldn't forget rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.22,
      "end_seconds": 283.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.85,
      "end_seconds": 317.26,
      "duration_seconds": 32.41,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like polymyalgia rheumatica, but I'd like to confirm. I think blood tests makes sense here, for proximal stiffness. Let's use prednisolone, 15 milligrams, once a day, reducing course. You take it by mouth. That should help with polymyalgia rheumatica. Report any headache or jaw pain immediately. I'll want another look in two weeks. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.8,
      "end_seconds": 320.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}